From: Manikanta Mylavarapu <manikanta.mylavarapu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom_scm: pass PAS metadata size on IPQ5332

Backport the v14 metadata-size change to Linux 6.18's existing PAS API.
Use command V2 only if TrustZone reports it available; retain the old
two-argument call for existing firmware/platforms. No generic PAS API
migration or unrelated watchdog formatting change is included.
Original: 20260803-rproc-v14-1-a1f87b0b0ad2@oss.qualcomm.com

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -662,6 +662,14 @@ int qcom_scm_pas_init_image(u32 pas_id, const void *metadata, size_t size,
 
 	desc.args[1] = mdata_phys;
 
+	if (__qcom_scm_is_call_available(__scm->dev, QCOM_SCM_SVC_PIL,
+					 QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2)) {
+		desc.cmd = QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2;
+		desc.arginfo = QCOM_SCM_ARGS(3, QCOM_SCM_VAL, QCOM_SCM_RW,
+					     QCOM_SCM_VAL);
+		desc.args[2] = size;
+	}
+
 	ret = qcom_scm_call(__scm->dev, &desc, &res);
 	qcom_scm_bw_disable();
 
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_SHUTDOWN	0x06
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_IS_SUPPORTED	0x07
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_MSS_RESET	0x0a
+#define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2	0x1a
 
 #define QCOM_SCM_SVC_IO			0x05
 #define QCOM_SCM_IO_READ		0x01
